sure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-79359" :question/id #uuid "04248f58-d370-5624-b1ab-718c32069b86" :question/math-academy-id "q-79359" :question/problem "Expressed in terms of ${log}_{4}$, what value of $x$ satisfies the equation ${4}^{x+1}={7}^{x}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take ${log}_{4}$ in both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{4}^{x+1} & ={7}^{x} \\\\ {log}_{4}⁡({4}^{x+1}) & ={log}_{4}⁡({7}^{x})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that ${log}_{4}⁡({4}^{c})=c$ to simplify the left-hand side. This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+1 & ={log}_{4}⁡({7}^{x})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we use the power law of logarithms to simplify the right-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+1 & ={log}_{4}⁡({7}^{x}) \\\\ x+1 & =x{log}_{4}⁡(7)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+1 & =x{log}_{4}⁡(7) \\\\ x-x{log}_{4}⁡(7) & =-1 \\\\ x(1-{log}_{4}⁡(7)) & =-1 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{1-{log}_{4}⁡(7)}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-79359/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7e37891e-d24f-53cd-ba74-d887fa99aa3b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-79359"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-242938/field-1/d1e76ca58a5b638983431d9fe7b3492f4d02377168cb2d8bff2928f2d4137352" :answer/id #uuid "3dda0191-cfab-52a8-984d-da80f345ebf4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\log(2)-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-242938/field-1/23a9eb8c083bc79d51213e33bd7c4212d28e3598554a36cbf9cd4c20e955ca1a" :answer/id #uuid "a780f4a0-8450-5cb8-805a-2dd97752953c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\log(2)+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-242938/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "1d20689e-f160-5519-ba1e-e161d006fcd5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-242938/field-1/d1e76ca58a5b638983431d9fe7b3492f4d02377168cb2d8bff2928f2d4137352" :answer-field/choices ["q-242938/field-1/d1e76ca58a5b638983431d9fe7b3492f4d02377168cb2d8bff2928f2d4137352" "q-242938/field-1/23a9eb8c083bc79d51213e33bd7c4212d28e3598554a36cbf9cd4c20e955ca1a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-242938" :question/id #uuid "a80e13c8-4b2d-570c-89d6-a9e588816f96" :question/math-academy-id "q-242938" :question/problem "Expressed in terms of common logarithms, what value of $x$ satisfies the equation ${10}^{x+1}={2}^{x}?$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the common logarithm $(log)$ of both sides of the equation: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{10}^{x+1} & ={2}^{x} \\\\ \\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{x+1}) & =\\operatorname{log}⁡({2}^{x})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that ${log}_{b}⁡({b}^{c})=c$ to simplify the left-hand side. This gives:\n\n$$\nx+1=\\operatorname{log}⁡({2}^{x})\n$$\n\nNext, we use the power law of logarithms to simplify the right-hand side:\n\n$$\nx+1=x\\operatorname{log}⁡(2)\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\operatorname{log}⁡(2)-x & =1 \\\\ x(\\operatorname{log}⁡(2)-1) & =1 \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{log}⁡(2)-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-242938/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7e37891e-d24f-53cd-ba74-d887fa99aa3b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-242938"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-26828/selection/2f835475e6d2d58b936ccab65b111f4ac09ab4ba8dd6752c23366ad03f9a890a" :answer/id #uuid "9b2c3f1f-ed08-5d4d-8b06-08b1901eb0c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6.213" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-26828/selection/7d2407fa6bf2fbf6d676d08ef39ac2fd5ab8a224ddf4139330e1e7aad84812f1" :answer/id #uuid "93b958a5-470b-501f-b39c-35b5c913a9af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5.891" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-26828/selection/2626b94f85323be7875e0e0d92ed664d29e27bea020941064192334424af85b4" :answer/id #uuid "604c19ce-2cf7-5112-b564-01e34a77f6d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.544" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-26828/selection/318a827479190b623edc64ad2ae29f1b507fab56c88eab6f6dbed127c0e8c751" :answer/id #uuid "3170abaf-55a7-547a-a014-f7d9e1d3ff68" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.293" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-26828/selection/f91d5577e5659e359a2b65255ce60071c63ad29b70fab98cc305557a0b5c91be" :answer/id #uuid "c30da09b-1dc2-51f6-ae45-e0ba1424e165" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7.712" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-26828/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1de15606-7cd8-52e0-9434-b6f499803b01" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-26828/selection/2f835475e6d2d58b936ccab65b111f4ac09ab4ba8dd6752c23366ad03f9a890a" :answer-field/choices ["q-26828/selection/2f835475e6d2d58b936ccab65b111f4ac09ab4ba8dd6752c23366ad03f9a890a" "q-26828/selection/7d2407fa6bf2fbf6d676d08ef39ac2fd5ab8a224ddf4139330e1e7aad84812f1" "q-26828/selection/2626b94f85323be7875e0e0d92ed664d29e27bea020941064192334424af85b4" "q-26828/selection/318a827479190b623edc64ad2ae29f1b507fab56c88eab6f6dbed127c0e8c751" "q-26828/selection/f91d5577e5659e359a2b65255ce60071c63ad29b70fab98cc305557a0b5c91be"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-26828" :question/id #uuid "c1b384d1-bf1d-5185-800b-b0cf5436aeb1" :question/math-academy-id "q-26828" :question/problem "Given that ${5}^{y}={4}^{y+1},$ what is the value of $y?$ Round your answer to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "First, we take ${log}_{5}$ on both sides of the equation: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{5}^{y}={4}^{y+1} \\\\ {log}_{5}⁡({5}^{y}) & ={log}_{5}⁡({4}^{y+1})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that ${log}_{b}⁡({b}^{c})=c$ to simplify the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={log}_{5}⁡({4}^{y+1})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we use the power law of logarithms to simplify the right-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =(y+1){log}_{5}⁡4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $y,$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =(y+1){log}_{5}⁡4 \\\\ y & =y{log}_{5}⁡4+{log}_{5}⁡4 \\\\ y-y{log}_{5}⁡4 & ={log}_{5}⁡4 \\\\ y(1-{log}_{5}⁡4) & ={log}_{5}⁡4 \\\\ y & =\\frac{{log}_{5}⁡4}{1-{log}_{5}⁡4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the change of base formula, we have\n\n$$\n{log}_{5}⁡(4)=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}≈0.861\\,353.\n$$\n\nFinally, then, we can approximate $y$ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y≈\\frac{0.861\\,353}{1-0.861\\,353}≈6.213,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nto $3$ decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-26828/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7e37891e-d24f-53cd-ba74-d887fa99aa3b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-26828"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-26385/selection/23f976a4f1982be9ec39a8c5701327a5906b08b13b99528f8a47d493c277199c" :answer/id #uuid "931a4ce6-7435-585c-9775-66d58253118b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{log}⁡(7)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-26385/selection/78cd6e57a6a4050db39c9ae3b4b7752c20c340447fbd20ea8666997ddc1031fe" :answer/id #uuid "42f06250-b7c9-580a-9166-2cfbdac14d2a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{\\operatorname{log}⁡(7)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-26385/selection/7ce76660cdce0d2f76f49bd8cb7aed377ed4b863889e467ddb5c64e06b40c7ba" :answer/id #uuid "60d37d82-ee94-569c-aaf8-e1423aeb7f4b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{\\operatorname{log}⁡(7)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-26385/selection/b5167274214d8cfc2c7e539d1edb1e1767bbfb80cee96eb821e50fee7db302b2" :answer/id #uuid "a6df1250-c2da-5c4f-8078-44a8901d5507" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{1-\\operatorname{log}⁡(7)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-26385/selection/6a39b62d5972d6ac2868769f1f451fd6394f03194598db8403c56e01f786e2a3" :answer/id #uuid "50ba0cd1-2629-5afe-ab11-6821ac544fce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{1+2\\operatorname{log}⁡(7)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-26385/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "49d093e8-d228-59bf-800a-810003a75896" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-26385/selection/b5167274214d8cfc2c7e539d1edb1e1767bbfb80cee96eb821e50fee7db302b2" :answer-field/choices ["q-26385/selection/23f976a4f1982be9ec39a8c5701327a5906b08b13b99528f8a47d493c277199c" "q-26385/selection/78cd6e57a6a4050db39c9ae3b4b7752c20c340447fbd20ea8666997ddc1031fe" "q-26385/selection/7ce76660cdce0d2f76f49bd8cb7aed377ed4b863889e467ddb5c64e06b40c7ba" "q-26385/selection/b5167274214d8cfc2c7e539d1edb1e1767bbfb80cee96eb821e50fee7db302b2" "q-26385/selection/6a39b62d5972d6ac2868769f1f451fd6394f03194598db8403c56e01f786e2a3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-26385" :question/id #uuid "ed7ab01a-8bb8-585b-9681-7e499c6dc236" :question/math-academy-id "q-26385" :question/problem "Expressed in terms of common logarithms, what value of $x$ satisfies the equation ${10}^{x-3}={7}^{x}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the common logarithm $(log)$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{10}^{x-3} & ={7}^{x} \\\\ \\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{x-3}) & =\\operatorname{log}⁡({7}^{x})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that ${log}_{b}⁡({b}^{c})=c$ to simplify the left-hand side. This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-3 & =\\operatorname{log}⁡({7}^{x})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we use the power law of logarithms to simplify the right-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-3 & =x\\operatorname{log}⁡(7)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-x\\operatorname{log}⁡(7) & =3 \\\\ x(1-\\operatorname{log}⁡(7)) & =3 \\\\ x & =\\frac{3}{1-\\operatorname{log}⁡(7)}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-26385/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7e37891e-d24f-53cd-ba74-d887fa99aa3b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-26385"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-242899/field-1/c474092ddc28caa16ab68fc15a435c31216ec4297d564eea44b9c30249d95c5c" :answer/id #uuid "b87f1ee2-1ef7-5b1c-b22c-96427b594c17" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.791" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-242899/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "2b1bdacb-07a0-5d62-a827-f3d945513621" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-242899/field-1/c474092ddc28caa16ab68fc15a435c31216ec4297d564eea44b9c30249d95c5c" :answer-field/choices ["q-242899/field-1/c474092ddc28caa16ab68fc15a435c31216ec4297d564eea44b9c30249d95c5c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-242899" :question/id #uuid "9fbe8518-3b94-57e7-a090-a9853e4fce38" :question/math-academy-id "q-242899" :question/problem "Given that ${8}^{1-x}={3}^{x/2},$ what is the value of $x?$ Round your answer to $3$ decimal places.\n\n$x≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we take ${log}_{8}$ on both sides of the equation: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{8}^{1-x} & ={3}^{x/2} \\\\ {log}_{8}⁡({8}^{1-x}) & ={log}_{8}⁡({3}^{x/2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we use the fact that ${log}_{b}⁡({b}^{c})=c$ to simplify the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n1-x={log}_{8}⁡({3}^{x/2})\n$$\n\nNext, we use the power law of logarithms to simplify the right-hand side:\n\n$$\n1-x=\\frac{x}{2}{log}_{8}⁡3\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $x,$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-x & =\\frac{x}{2}{log}_{8}⁡3 \\\\ 1 & =x+\\frac{x}{2}{log}_{8}⁡3 \\\\ x+\\frac{x}{2}{log}_{8}⁡3 & =1 \\\\ 2x+x{log}_{8}⁡3 & =2 \\\\ x(2+{log}_{8}⁡3) & =2 \\\\ x & =\\frac{2}{2+{log}_{8}⁡3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the change of base formula, we have\n\n$$\n{log}_{8}⁡(3)=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8)}≈0.528\\,321.\n$$\n\nFinally,  we can approximate $x$ as \n\n$$\nx≈\\frac{2}{2+0.528\\,321}≈0.791,\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-242899/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7e37891e-d24f-53cd-ba74-d887fa99aa3b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-242899"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-110545/selection/73175fd5988a945a3c3de8acc1851eb36199f8394df07fd7265e49f2aef8940b" :answer/id #uuid "0c792d3e-7096-5d22-b213-f53e91a6409d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110545/selection/c9e9b76971fbe0beb66f317fed229a9d09022e3ef2d1c7c8b00004bab007ec11" :answer/id #uuid "988dc7fb-e0a5-5faa-b378-00b15774a54d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110545/selection/0b3e67e2467a97ee1c4e234dcf7d4dd182df519b77dc6c32175781a03bb5537a" :answer/id #uuid "0fcaebca-cab8-533b-8890-7b9e1f628c87" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8)}{1+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110545/selection/f74e383016e8ec70480014a3f074b2d8dc5d1dc41e2e3f01d4b8dd8ea7351abf" :answer/id #uuid "203dd4eb-be6e-59cd-add0-497d7e174b05" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110545/selection/cc0bd931cb40a79403d6360beb19c97db17044cdc5f323eefd640ca0cb639aff" :answer/id #uuid "0d1e9b47-3151-5f52-a03d-a411a0b05931" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110545/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2e6162b3-6a3d-59f3-87d1-504aa5c92d11" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-110545/selection/0b3e67e2467a97ee1c4e234dcf7d4dd182df519b77dc6c32175781a03bb5537a" :answer-field/choices ["q-110545/selection/73175fd5988a945a3c3de8acc1851eb36199f8394df07fd7265e49f2aef8940b" "q-110545/selection/c9e9b76971fbe0beb66f317fed229a9d09022e3ef2d1c7c8b00004bab007ec11" "q-110545/selection/0b3e67e2467a97ee1c4e234dcf7d4dd182df519b77dc6c32175781a03bb5537a" "q-110545/selection/f74e383016e8ec70480014a3f074b2d8dc5d1dc41e2e3f01d4b8dd8ea7351abf" "q-110545/selection/cc0bd931cb40a79403d6360beb19c97db17044cdc5f323eefd640ca0cb639aff"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-110545" :question/id #uuid "47457fc5-4715-5250-8afb-4edbb48c0413" :question/math-academy-id "q-110545" :question/problem "Expressed in terms of natural logarithms, what value of $y$ satisfies the equation ${e}^{y}={8}^{1-2y}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the natural logarithm $(ln)$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{y} & ={8}^{1-2y} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{y}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({8}^{1-2y})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that $\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{a})=a$ to simplify the left-hand side. This gives:\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({8}^{1-2y})\n$$\n\nFinally, we use the power law of logarithms to simplify the right-hand side:\n\n$$\ny=(1-2y)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8)\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $y$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =(1-2y)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8) \\\\ y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8)-2y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8) \\\\ y+2y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8) \\\\ y(1+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8)) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8) \\\\ y & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8)}{1+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8)}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-110545/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5eb24b54-bdb8-5269-bd38-d346a52bbc6e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-110545"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-66899/selection/1ec66e3303ab624cbde80a0ec13b70d34c2a84328d373dbb368b02366c1a2854" :answer/id #uuid "281ac056-8d00-568b-897e-3a824bf12ac4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-66899/selection/2136feb3b3a72c8dddb076fcc559dfc3a867d041ef123ab3207997711ad359ee" :answer/id #uuid "bddf0bc8-6186-5921-aa31-f0376dcf91cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-66899/selection/55578343325e6fcc08499d1876c91da01fd0d441efeadf890e3f407a22421e9f" :answer/id #uuid "a3dc6907-0543-5f80-b778-98317f9bc61e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(9)-3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-66899/selection/3af1adf59f868fdb863961d809a22b16c145ed516221e29060504cbdac2e8fb2" :answer/id #uuid "7ae3b9a2-69ab-5139-8a18-2c9b64fc5911" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-66899/selection/680bcc16a78e3aa1b9751274948c3c664bd268e98394ccadafc019d89964c861" :answer/id #uuid "c755523e-15e7-582b-8b1d-e426d69c1602" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)-1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-66899/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0a422cf4-3bc3-590f-a7e8-750f4534bb3e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-66899/selection/3af1adf59f868fdb863961d809a22b16c145ed516221e29060504cbdac2e8fb2" :answer-field/choices ["q-66899/selection/1ec66e3303ab624cbde80a0ec13b70d34c2a84328d373dbb368b02366c1a2854" "q-66899/selection/2136feb3b3a72c8dddb076fcc559dfc3a867d041ef123ab3207997711ad359ee" "q-66899/selection/55578343325e6fcc08499d1876c91da01fd0d441efeadf890e3f407a22421e9f" "q-66899/selection/3af1adf59f868fdb863961d809a22b16c145ed516221e29060504cbdac2e8fb2" "q-66899/selection/680bcc16a78e3aa1b9751274948c3c664bd268e98394ccadafc019d89964c861"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-66899" :question/id #uuid "3907caa8-855e-5e3e-bfcf-8820788b0b2b" :question/math-academy-id "q-66899" :question/problem "Expressed in terms of natural logarithms, what value of $y$ satisfies the equation ${e}^{y+1}={3}^{2y}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the natural logarithm $(ln)$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{y+1} & ={3}^{2y} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{y+1}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({3}^{2y})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that $\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{a})=a$ to simplify the left-hand side. This gives:\n\n$$\ny+1=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({3}^{2y})\\,\n$$\n\nNext, we use the power and product laws of logarithms to simplify the right-hand side:\n\n$$\ny+1=2y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $y$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+1 & =2y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3) \\\\ 2y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)-y & =1 \\\\ y(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)-1) & =1 \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-66899/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5eb24b54-bdb8-5269-bd38-d346a52bbc6e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-66899"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-79361/selection/d2ea4e40226e8509872acbf2dda3a783358a91b3b640fce043b26637da1db08a" :answer/id #uuid "4142750c-fb70-57d9-8eec-97746c2be1f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79361/selection/edf7eff564d259838aaf141c69093c929d59dc87aba65905ad8b5be95ec85b62" :answer/id #uuid "e496457e-5e24-5720-8c16-e71ba3af5128" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5+1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79361/selection/86acdfdc2c1c402580b9792e323cfea62b8762285203f856a996af6f84c68e4a" :answer/id #uuid "8ba7bed8-2fcb-5ce